{"reference":"1 Chronicles 25","book":"1 Chronicles","chapter":25,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Wider Administrative Setting","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"This chapter’s detailed ordering of temple musicians belongs to a larger set of Levitical, musical, and administrative arrangements in the surrounding chapters. These arrangements may preserve earlier traditions while also reflecting and authorizing later temple institutions, so their direct projection onto a single moment in David’s reign remains historically disputed.","verse_refs":["1 Chronicles 23:1-32","1 Chronicles 24:1-31","1 Chronicles 26:1-32","1 Chronicles 27:1-34"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_chronicles_025_d5f12d08f4601c09376bf237"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}